+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Clients want to send only what changed between two versions of a JSON document, not the whole new version. The library can apply RFC 6902 patches but cannot produce them.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returning an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`.
+- The patch is minimal in scope: only the parts that differ are addressed; unchanged members and elements are never mentioned.
+- Neither input is mutated, and the patch shares no mutable structure with them.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch-diff`: generating a JSON Patch from two JSON values.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+New `src/diff.ts` and tests, plus an export in `src/index.ts`. No change to existing behaviour.
